---
// src/pages/about.astro
// What this is, what it isn't, what the methodology is in plain English.
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — RTFP</title>
    <style>
      :root { --bg: #fafaf9; --ink: #1c1917; --ink-dim: #57534e; --ink-faint: #78716c; --border: #e7e5e4; }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { margin: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.6; }
      header, main, footer { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
      header { padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
      header h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; }
      header nav { margin-top: 1rem; display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-dim); }
      header nav a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
      header nav a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
      main { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
      main h2 { font-size: 2rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      main h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
      main p { color: var(--ink-dim); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      footer { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-faint); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <h1>RTFP</h1>
      <nav>
        <a href="/">Findings</a>
        <a href="/sources">Sources</a>
        <a href="/about">About</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>
        RTFP is a cross-platform comparison of the largest platforms'
        EU Digital Services Act transparency reports. The site loads the
        platforms' published filings into a normalised database and exposes
        the comparisons no individual provider reports themselves.
      </p>

      <h3>Why now</h3>
      <p>
        The DSA has required VLOPs and VLOSEs to publish transparency
        reports twice a year since August 2023. For the first two years, every
        platform reported in its own format — comparison was nearly impossible.
        From the H2 2025 reporting cycle (published February 2026), all VLOPs
        must use the harmonised template defined by Commission Implementing
        Regulation 2024/2835. This is the first time the major platforms can be
        compared directly.
      </p>

      <h3>What's covered</h3>
      <p>
        Our initial trial dataset covers the H2 2025 filings of TikTok, Instagram,
        LinkedIn, and X. The dataset will grow over time, as new reports are
        filed - the next cycle covering H1 2026 is due in August 2026 - and any
        amendments to past filings will be added when issued.
      </p>

      <h3>What this is not</h3>
      <p>
        This is not an audit. Every number on the site is what each
        platform self-reported. Where platforms disagree on methodology — and they
        do — we note that as a finding rather than picking a winner.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site does not include data from the EU's Statements of Reasons
        database (which is a separate dataset covering individual moderation
        decisions). This site covers only the quantitative templates filed under Articles
        15 and 24 of the DSA, and the qualitative narrative sections under Article 42.
      </p>

      <h3>How the numbers reconcile</h3>
      <p>
        Each finding on the site links to the underlying database view. Every view
        is publicly queryable via the REST API; the URL on the home page footer
        leads to the full reference. Every filing the site draws from is linked on
        the Sources page so the numbers can be checked against the providers'
        own published reports.
      </p>

      <h3>Who built this</h3>
      <p>
        Oscar and Sune [@]
      </p>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>Questions, corrections, suggestions: [contact to come].</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>